# Stacking effects, most of them off.
#
# The point of this script is what it does NOT cost. Every stage below is
# available, and a stage whose settings would change nothing is skipped
# entirely -- no allocation, no dispatch, no copy. Its output aliases its
# input, so the pixels flow straight through.
#
# That is what makes a long stack practical. Twenty effects with three in use
# allocates three intermediates, not twenty, and at 45 MP that is the
# difference between a usable pipeline and one that pages.
#
# Watch the status line: it says how many stages were bypassed, so "did that
# actually skip?" is answerable rather than a matter of faith.
#
# Set any of these to its neutral value and the stage disappears from the run:
#   gaussian_blur   sigma  = 0
#   brightness      brightness = 0 and gain = 1
#   wavelet_denoise luma = 0 and chroma = 0

src = image("test")

src => params( gaussian_blur )()
    => params( brightness )()
    => params( wavelet_denoise )()
    => display( "stacked" )
